  "verbalization": "Amiloride, through its indication for Congestive Heart Failure, appears to be linked to Hypertension via a chain of drug-indication relationships. This connection is supported by the shared pathway from Amiloride to Congestive Heart Failure, which in turn is associated with Hypertension through multiple drugs (Indapamide, Piretanide, and Hydroflumethiazide). These drugs are all known to contribute to blood pressure regulation, suggesting a potential mechanism involving sodium retention or vasodilation. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a broader, underlying relationship between Amiloride and Hypertension. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Congestive Heart Failure as a mediator, with Amiloride potentially influencing blood pressure through its effects on heart function and fluid balance.",
